只需通过该联系页面即可。

00:42:00.996 --> 00:42:01.496
Wow.
哇。

00:42:01.496 --> 00:42:02.198
It's amazing.
太棒了。

00:42:02.198 --> 00:42:15.753
Can I also say like if you're loving this podcast and certain friends and family members who love how I made my mother are not listening, can And we ask our listeners to give them a little nudge and send them the link and say I'm really enjoying this.
我也可以说，如果你喜欢这个播客，而某些喜欢我如何让我母亲做的朋友和家人没有听，我们可以要求我们的听众给他们一点推动，并向他们发送链接，并说我真的很喜欢这个。

00:42:15.469 --> 00:42:25.909
We would love to get our army of how we made your mother supporters and lovers out there turning people on to what we're doing here because we're having such a good time.
我们很乐意让我们的军队了解我们如何让你的母亲成为支持者和爱人，让人们关注我们在这里所做的事情，因为我们玩得很开心。

00:42:25.909 --> 00:42:30.949
And we love whoever's listening to this right now, but we would also love more people to tune in if they love the show.
我们喜欢现在正在听这个节目的人，但我们也希望更多的人喜欢这个节目，来收听。

00:42:30.949 --> 00:42:33.349
We also have a lovely letter that we're going to read, right, Alec?
我们还有一封可爱的信要读，对吧，亚历克？

00:42:33.349 --> 00:42:34.349
Yes, indeed.
是的，确实如此。

00:42:34.349 --> 00:42:35.349
Go for it.
大胆试试吧。

00:42:35.349 --> 00:42:37.789
And I will take the lead on this one today.
今天我将带头解决这一问题。

00:42:37.789 --> 00:42:38.789
I have not read this.
我还没有读过这个。

00:42:38.789 --> 00:42:42.309
So I'm going to be surprised as we go.
所以当我们去的时候我会感到惊讶。

00:42:42.309 --> 00:42:43.309
Dear Josh and Craig.
亲爱的乔什和克雷格。

00:42:43.309 --> 00:42:44.309
Oh my God.
我的天啊。

00:42:44.309 --> 00:42:45.309
No, I'm kidding.
不，我在开玩笑。

00:42:45.309 --> 00:42:46.309
That didn't surprise me.
这并不令我惊讶。

00:42:46.309 --> 00:42:47.309
Dear Josh and Craig.
亲爱的乔什和克雷格。

00:42:47.309 --> 00:42:48.309
My name is Mateo.
我叫马特奥。

00:42:48.309 --> 00:42:52.309
I'm an almost 30 year old Italian guy who grew up with your show.
我是一个快 30 岁的意大利人，是伴随着你们的节目长大的。

00:42:52.309 --> 00:42:56.599
And this podcast is truly an incredible gift for me.
这个播客对我来说确实是一份不可思议的礼物。

00:42:56.599 --> 00:43:02.239
Last year I had the chance to chat with Josh after the beautiful play the ally at the public theater in New York.
去年，在纽约公共剧院演出《盟友》之后，我有机会与乔什聊天。

00:43:02.239 --> 00:43:03.239
Oh, that's so nice.
哦，那太好了。

00:43:03.239 --> 00:43:05.239
Glad he saw it.
很高兴他看到了。

00:43:05.239 --> 00:43:16.880
I was almost embarrassed because it didn't feel right to talk about how I made a mother after he had just performed in another production, but for me, it was my only chance to tell him what the show has meant to me and how important it still is in my life.
我几乎感到尴尬，因为在他刚刚在另一部作品中表演后谈论我如何成为一名母亲感觉不太合适，但对我来说，这是我唯一的机会告诉他这部剧对我意味着什么以及它在我的生活中仍然有多重要。

00:43:16.880 --> 00:43:19.639
I started watching him yum when I was a teenager.
当我十几岁的时候，我就开始看他的表演了。

00:43:19.639 --> 00:43:26.280
While the fifth season was airing in the US, I was discovering the pilot episode, and from that moment on, I never let go of it.
当第五季在美国播出时，我正在探索试播集，从那一刻起，我就再也没有放过它。

00:43:26.280 --> 00:43:28.280
In fact, it became a part of me.
事实上，它已经成为我的一部分。

00:43:28.280 --> 00:43:34.599
As I grew up, him yum was always there, my happy place to retreat to when things were going wrong.
在我的成长过程中，他总是在那里，当事情出错时，他是我快乐的避难所。

00:43:34.599 --> 00:43:44.199
In 2014, the very year of the final season, I completed my studies and found myself facing bigger enemies, anxiety and depression.
2014年，也就是最后一季的那一年，我完成了学业，发现自己面临着更大的敌人、焦虑和抑郁。

00:43:44.199 --> 00:43:46.679
During those difficult times, him and him was there for me.
在那些困难的时刻，他和他一直在我身边。

00:43:46.679 --> 00:43:51.440
The show became in a way and anchor that accompanied me through the darkest periods.
该节目成为陪伴我度过最黑暗时期的一种方式和锚。

00:43:51.440 --> 00:43:53.079
So I started writing a book.
所以我开始写一本书。

00:43:53.079 --> 00:43:56.519
I set the project aside because I wasn't satisfied with what I had written.
我搁置了这个项目，因为我对自己写的内容不满意。

00:43:56.519 --> 00:44:05.690
Over the following years, I realized that the real change had to come from within facing my depression with the help of a psychologist, not with DIY remedies.
在接下来的几年里，我意识到真正的改变必须来自内心，在心理学家的帮助下面对我的抑郁症，而不是DIY疗法。

00:44:05.690 --> 00:44:12.610
I don't want to go into the details of my life or therapy, but a few years ago, when I found the draft of the novel, I decided to pick it up again.
我不想谈论我的生活或治疗的细节，但几年前，当我发现小说的草稿时，我决定再次拿起它。

00:44:12.610 --> 00:44:24.250
This letter is simply to thank you for being a part of my life for so many years and for inspiring my book, which in 2023 was selected by a publisher and officially released in bookstores all over Italy.
这封信只是为了感谢您多年来成为我生活的一部分，并为我的书提供了灵感，这本书于2023年被一家出版商选中，并在意大利各地的书店正式发行。

00:44:24.250 --> 00:44:27.298
called Il Suppore della Vita, the flavor of life.
称为“Il Suppore della Vita”，即生活的味道。

00:44:27.298 --> 00:44:29.413
Forgive me if I mispronounce that.
如果我发音错误，请原谅我。

00:44:29.413 --> 00:44:33.083
And while it's written by me, there's so much of you in it.
虽然它是我写的，但里面有很多你们。

00:44:33.083 --> 00:44:33.583
Oh, my.
哦，我的。

00:44:33.583 --> 00:44:34.516
That's so nice.
那太好了。

00:44:34.516 --> 00:44:38.683
Thank you for creating something that went beyond a simple dramedy.
感谢您创作了超越简单喜剧的作品。

00:44:38.683 --> 00:44:43.971
How I met your mother has been and continues to be a piece of my life with affection.
我如何认识你母亲一直并将继续成为我充满感情的生活的一部分。

00:44:43.971 --> 00:44:44.904
Mateo Kamarata.
马特奥·卡马拉塔。

00:44:44.904 --> 00:44:45.899
That's the best.
那是最好的。

00:44:45.899 --> 00:44:46.399
Wow.
哇。

00:44:46.399 --> 00:44:47.208
Thanks Mateo.
谢谢马特奥。

00:44:47.208 --> 00:44:48.825
Mateo, thank you for that.
马特奥，谢谢你。

00:44:49.340 --> 00:44:49.840
Thank you.
谢谢。

00:44:49.840 --> 00:44:50.928
That's really beautiful.
那真的很漂亮。

00:44:50.928 --> 00:44:53.104
It's the letters like that have been so amazing.
这样的字母真是太神奇了。

00:44:53.104 --> 00:44:56.413
One an honor that the show meant that to people, please keep them coming.
一个荣幸的是，这个节目对人们来说意味着，请让他们继续来。

00:44:56.413 --> 00:44:57.546
Mateo, thank you so much.
马特奥，非常感谢你。

00:44:57.500 --> 00:44:58.689
Congrats on the novel.
恭喜小说。

00:44:58.689 --> 00:44:59.500
Yeah, congrats.
是的，恭喜。

00:44:59.500 --> 00:45:00.645
Check out Mateo's novel.
看看马特奥的小说。

00:45:00.645 --> 00:45:02.219
That's really the flavor of life.
这真是生活的味道。

00:45:02.219 --> 00:45:03.743
Glad to show help to you.
很高兴为您提供帮助。

00:45:03.743 --> 00:45:10.871
And I also think, you know, like I said, Greg earlier, like you, you and Carter wrote characters who were vulnerable.
我还认为，你知道，就像我之前说的，格雷格，就像你一样，你和卡特写的角色都是脆弱的。

00:45:10.871 --> 00:45:17.269
And I think, you know, there's this idea that we're supposed to show our toughest self and our best self.
我认为，你知道，有这样一种想法，我们应该展示我们最坚强的自我和最好的自我。

00:45:17.269 --> 00:45:22.021
But true connection is formed when we reveal our wounds and our vulnerability.
但当我们揭露自己的伤口和脆弱性时，真正的联系就会形成。

00:45:22.021 --> 00:45:23.910
That's where we really connect.
这就是我们真正联系的地方。

00:45:23.910 --> 00:45:34.390
So I think what he's saying in this letter is that we helped him get in touch with those tender spots, where his nerve endings were exposed, and he really needed some help.
所以我认为他在这封信中所说的是我们帮助他接触到那些暴露的敏感点，他的神经末梢暴露在外，他确实需要一些帮助。

00:45:34.390 --> 00:45:35.547
It's just such a...
就是这样一个...

00:45:35.547 --> 00:45:45.235
You don't realize what you're doing for people just by telling a story that is going to help them reflect and metabolize their their lives and their struggles.
仅仅通过讲述一个帮助人们反思和代谢他们的生活和挣扎的故事，你并没有意识到你在为人们做什么。

00:45:45.235 --> 00:45:56.811
So this is a perfect example of like, I mean, to inspire someone to, to, to, to be there a company, to accompany them through the dark moments of their life and also inspire them creatively.
所以这是一个完美的例子，我的意思是，激励某人加入一家公司，陪伴他们度过人生的黑暗时刻，并激发他们的创造力。

00:45:56.811 --> 00:46:01.015
I can't imagine a better thing to do of a work of art, be able to do.
我无法想象能够对一件艺术品做更好的事情。

00:46:01.015 --> 00:46:02.904
Yeah, it's, it's why you do it.
是的，这就是你这样做的原因。

00:46:02.904 --> 00:46:09.972
It's the, the hope in the dream, like talking about this episode, but Ted has this, this faith, right in this dream.
这是梦中的希望，就像谈论这一集一样，但特德在这个梦中拥有这个、这个信念。

00:46:09.972 --> 00:46:14.419
He's up up there on the top of that roof, waiting for the slutty pumpkin.
他在屋顶上，等待放荡的南瓜。

00:46:14.420 --> 00:46:20.300
And I was like, you know, this almost unreasonable level of faith that it will all mean something one day.
我当时想，你知道，这种几乎不合理的信念，相信有一天这一切都会有意义。

00:46:20.300 --> 00:46:24.820
And that's the same faith you have when you write something you make already put it out into the world.
当你写出一些已经发布到世界各地的东西时，你也有同样的信念。

00:46:24.820 --> 00:46:31.539
And the idea that the show has gone out there and connected with people like Mateo in that way, it's really, it's so humbling.
想到这部剧已经播出并以这种方式与马特奥这样的人建立了联系，真的，这真是太令人谦卑了。

00:46:31.539 --> 00:46:37.739
And like, you dream of that when you start a project and when it happens, it's just, it's a dream come true.
就像，当你开始一个项目时你就梦想着这一点，当它发生时，那就是梦想成真了。

00:46:37.739 --> 00:46:39.139
So thank you, thank you, Mateo.
所以谢谢你，谢谢你，马特奥。

00:46:39.139 --> 00:46:41.579
Thank you everybody for sharing these stories.
感谢大家分享这些故事。

00:46:41.579 --> 00:46:42.900
That means the world to us.
这对我们来说意味着世界。

00:46:42.900 --> 00:46:43.739
Thanks, Matteo.
谢谢，马特奥。

00:46:43.739 --> 00:46:44.500
That was really beautiful.
那真是太美了。

00:46:44.500 --> 00:46:45.880
Thank you.
谢谢。

